.TH MU2EDAQ-REAPER 1 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-reaper \- command line client for mu2edaq-file-reaper instances
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-reaper
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.PP
.B mu2edaq-reaper
[\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR | \fB\-\-instance\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
[\fB\-\-admin\-token\fR \fISECRET\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIcommand\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq-reaper
talks to the REST API of a running
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1)
over HTTP.  It uses only the Python standard library, so it runs from any
node on the DAQ network.  Output is a readable table by default and the raw
API JSON with
.BR \-\-json .
.PP
The server is found from
.BR \-\-url ,
else from
.B \-\-instance
through mu2edaq-discovery (matching the instance
.I label
each reaper advertises), else from the environment or configuration file,
else
.IR http://localhost:5004 .
The bearer token comes from
.BR \-\-token ,
the environment, or the per-URL token cache filled by
.BR "token login" .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Reaper base URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-instance " LABEL"
Find the reaper by instance label via mu2edaq-discovery.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Bearer token (default: environment, then cache).
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-token " SECRET"
The server's admin secret; only needed to mint the first API token or when
no token is available for an admin command.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
HTTP timeout (default 10).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the raw API JSON.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Client YAML configuration file (keys
.IR url ", " instance ", " timeout ", " token_file ", " discovery_timeout ).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the client version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Health, summary counts and one line per area.  Exit status 1 when the server
reports itself degraded.
.TP
.B areas
Table of every area.
.TP
.BI area " NAME"
Details of one area: usage, tiers with trigger/stop points and bytes to the
stop point, active tier, queue sizes, last scan, progress, rejection counts,
warnings.
.TP
.BI pause " NAME" " [\-\-reason " TEXT ]
Pause reaping of an area: scans continue and queues are published, but
nothing is compressed or deleted.  Requires the
.I operate
scope.
.TP
.BI resume " NAME" " [\-\-reason " TEXT ]
Resume a paused area and request a scan.
.TP
.BI disable " NAME" " [\-\-reason " TEXT ]
Disable an area entirely (no scans).  Requires
.IR admin .
.TP
.BI enable " NAME" " [\-\-reason " TEXT ]
Re-enable a disabled area.  Requires
.IR admin .
.TP
.BI rescan " NAME"
Request an immediate scan.
.TP
.BI plan " NAME" " [\-\-limit " N ]
Run a dry-run scan now and print the report and the top queue entries.
Nothing is modified.
.TP
.BR queues " [\-\-area " \fIA\fR "] [\-\-kind compress|delete] [\-\-status " \fIS\fR "] [\-\-limit " \fIN\fR ]
List queued entries across areas.
.TP
.BI "exclude add" " PATTERN" " [\-\-area " A "] [\-\-kind path|glob] [\-\-reason " TEXT "] [\-\-expires\-in " DURATION ]
Add an exclusion (absolute path, directory prefix or glob).  Excluded files
are never queued; an exclusion added while a queue is being worked takes
effect before the next file.
.TP
.BI "exclude rm" " ID"
Deactivate an exclusion.
.TP
.BR "exclude list" " [\-\-area " \fIA\fR "] [\-\-all]"
List exclusions.
.TP
.BR history " [\-\-area " \fIA\fR "] [\-\-path " \fIGLOB\fR "] [\-\-type " \fIT1,T2\fR "] [\-\-tier " \fIT\fR "] [\-\-since " \fITS\fR "] [\-\-until " \fITS\fR "] [\-\-limit " \fIN\fR "] [\-\-offset " \fIN\fR "] [\-\-asc] [\-\-csv " \fIFILE\fR "] [\-\-types]"
Query the audit history.
.B \-\-since
and
.B \-\-until
accept ISO-8601 or a relative duration such as
.BR 24h .
.B \-\-csv \-
writes CSV to stdout;
.B \-\-types
lists the event types.
.TP
.BR "notify test" " [" \fICHANNEL\fR "] [\-\-severity info|warning|critical]"
Send a test notification through one or every channel (admin).
.TP
.BR "notify status" " [\-\-limit " \fIN\fR ]
Channel status and recent sends.
.TP
.BI "token create" " NAME" " [\-\-scopes " S1,S2 "] [\-\-expires\-in " DURATION "] [\-\-save]"
Mint a new API token (scopes
.IR read ", " operate ", " admin ;
default read).  The plaintext is printed once;
.B \-\-save
also stores it in the cache for this URL.  Uses the admin secret or an
admin-scoped bearer token.
.TP
.BR "token list" " [\-\-all]"
List tokens (admin).
.TP
.BI "token revoke" " ID"
Revoke a token (admin).
.TP
.BR "token login" " [" \fITOKEN\fR "] [\-\-name " \fILABEL\fR ]
Store a token in the cache for this URL (prompted when omitted) and verify
it against the server.
.TP
.B token logout
Forget the cached token for this URL.
.TP
.B token whoami
Show the identity and scopes the server sees for the current token.
.TP
.BR instances " [\-\-discovery\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR ]
Discover every file-reaper instance on the network (needs mu2edaq-discovery).
.TP
.BR config " [\-\-local]"
Show the server configuration, or the client's resolved settings and where
each came from.
.TP
.BR version " [\-\-local]"
Client and server versions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for an API or usage error (including 401 and 403, which
print a hint about
.BR "token login" );
2 when the server cannot be reached.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_URL
Base URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_INSTANCE
Instance label to look up via discovery.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_TOKEN
Bearer token; overrides the cache.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_ADMIN_TOKEN
Admin secret.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_TIMEOUT
HTTP timeout.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_CONFIG
Client configuration file.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_REAPER_TOKEN_FILE
Token cache location.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mu2edaq/file-reaper/tokens.yaml
Token cache, one entry per URL.  Created with mode 0600 in a 0700 directory;
the client refuses to read it when it is group- or world-readable.
.TP
.IR ./mu2edaq-reaper.yaml ", " ./config/mu2edaq-reaper.yaml ", " ~/.config/mu2edaq/file-reaper/cli.yaml ", " /etc/mu2edaq/file-reaper-cli.yaml
Client configuration search path.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mint the first token with the server's admin secret and cache it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq-reaper --url http://mu2e-dl-01:5004 --admin-token "$SECRET" \\
    token create ops --scopes read,operate,admin --save
.fi
.RE
.PP
Look at the data logger and pause raw-data reaping during a calibration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq-reaper --instance dl-01 status
mu2edaq-reaper --instance dl-01 area data-raw
mu2edaq-reaper --instance dl-01 pause data-raw --reason "calibration run"
.fi
.RE
.PP
What would the reaper do right now?
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq-reaper plan data-raw --limit 50
.fi
.RE
.PP
Everything deleted in the last day, as CSV:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq-reaper history --type action_delete --since 24h --csv - > deleted.csv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-api (7),
.BR mu2edaq-discover (1)
